I know exactly why this is happening!
When the red error text ("Required: Select a posting date") appears below the Date Picker, it makes the Date Picker component physically taller. Because the container holding both the Date Picker and the Button is set to vertically center its items (alignItems: "center"), it pushes the Button down to try and stay in the middle of that new height!
To fix this, we need to tell that specific container to align items to the **top** (flex-start) instead of the center. This way, the input box and the button stay perfectly aligned at the top, and the red text just hangs down below without moving the button.
### The Fix
Scroll down to where your Date Picker and Upload Button are side-by-side (around line 400).
**Find this exact line:**
```javascript
              <Box sx={{ ...boxCenterStyle, flexDirection: "row", mt: 2 }} onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}>

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
              <Box sx={{ ...boxCenterStyle, flexDirection: "row", alignItems: "flex-start", mt: 2 }} onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}>

```
By adding alignItems: "flex-start", the tops of both boxes will lock together perfectly, regardless of whether the error text is showing or hidden!
